  "step_3": "The decision reason requires (1) treating outcome differences as negligible and (2) preferring the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome. Step 1 showed that B has a higher probability (50% vs 25%) of a non-zero outcome, so the reason would favor B. However, in the verbal report, the individual explicitly considers the outcome magnitudes (6000 vs. 4000/2000), indicating that differences are not negligible to them. Moreover, they justify choosing A (the lower-probability lottery) due to its higher potential payoff and greater risk, which contradicts the reason's rule of preferring higher probability of winning. The information considered (outcome size, risk-taking) and the justification (higher reward justifies lower odds) do not align with the reason's focus on maximizing the chance of any win while ignoring outcome size. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
